ecause the points of \\(T_k\\) satisfy \\(2\\le s\\le k+1\\), the values of \\(t\\) for which a point of the line lies in \\(T_k\\) form an interval of length at most  \n\n   \\[\n   \\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k-1}{|\\Delta|}\\Bigr\\rfloor .\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n\n   Moreover, each step changes the two coordinates by \\(|q|\\) and \\(|p|\\) respectively, both at least\u202f1.  \n   If we move \\(t\\) steps in the direction that increases the sum, then both coordinates increase by at least \\(t\\).  \n   Since for any point of \\(T_k\\) we have \\(a+b\\le k+1\\), we obtain  \n\n   \\[\n   2t\\le k-1\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad t\\le\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k-1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n   Combining (5) and (6) gives the universal bound  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\text{Every sunny line contains at most }\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\text{ points of }T_k.}\n   \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Necessary condition on\u202f\\(k\\).**  \n   If the \\(k\\) sunny lines cover all \\(|T_k|=\\frac{k(k+1)}2\\) points, then by (7)\n\n   \\[\n   k\\cdot\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\ge\\frac{k(k+1)}2 .\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n\n   Dividing by the positive integer \\(k\\) yields  \n\n   \\[\n   \\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{k+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor\\ge\\frac{k+1}{2}.\n   \\tag{9}\n   \\]\n\n   Equality in (9) holds **iff** \\(\\frac{k+1}{2}\\) is an integer, i.e. **\\(k\\) is odd**.  \n   The degenerate case \\(k=0\\) trivially satisfies (8).  \n   Hence a necessary condition is  \n\n   \\[\n   k=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad k\\text{ odd},\\qquad 0\\le k\\le n .\n   \\tag{10}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Explicit constructions for the admissible values that I can verify completely.**  \n\n   *\\(k=0\\).*  \n   Take the \\(n\\) vertical lines \\(x=1,\\dots ,x=n\\).  \n   None of them is sunny, and each point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) lies on the line \\(x=a\\).\n\n   *\\(k=1\\).*  \n   Use the single sunny line \\(y=x\\) together with the \\(n-1\\) vertical lines \\(x=2,\\dots 